# Subproject skills

This project splits skills by folder. **Read that side's `SKILL.md` before writing or changing code.**

| Folder | Skill to read |
|--------|----------------|
| `design/**` | `.cursor/skills/design/SKILL.md` |
| `frontend/**` | `.cursor/skills/frontend/SKILL.md` |
| `backend/**`, `infrastructure/**` | `.cursor/skills/backend/SKILL.md` |
| `document/postman/**` or API test / Postman work | `.cursor/skills/tester/SKILL.md` |

Notes:

- `design/schema/` = human-readable table definitions (SQL) — the design skill uses them for mock data shape; the backend skill turns them into real migrations
- `design/schema/` IDs are `BIGSERIAL`/`BIGINT` (not UUID); new backend migrations follow design schema when adding tables
- Any change to system behavior → follow `.cursor/rules/document.mdc` and update `document/` (checklist / knowledge / postman) in the same turn
- Phase checklists live under `document/checklist/<area>/` where `<area>` is `design`, `frontend`, `backend`, or `infrastructure`
- Cross-cutting work → read every related skill
- **Tables / lists** → follow [`.cursor/rules/tables.mdc`](tables.mdc) (pagination + sort order)
- **Forms** → follow [`.cursor/rules/forms.mdc`](forms.mdc)
- **Date/datetime display** → follow [`.cursor/rules/dates.mdc`](dates.mdc)
- **Warehouse layout / item placement** → follow [`.cursor/rules/warehouse.mdc`](warehouse.mdc) (bin-only `product_item_warehouse`)
- **Frontend component reuse** → follow [`.cursor/rules/storybook.mdc`](storybook.mdc) (Storybook as baseline)
- **Frontend layer stack** → follow [`.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc`](design-system.mdc) (tokens → shadcn → atomic → pages)
- **Frontend `components/` changes** → atomic reuse gate + user approval for new shared UI ([design-system.mdc](design-system.mdc)); run `make frontend-storybook-build` before done ([storybook.mdc](storybook.mdc))
- Invoke directly with `/design`, `/frontend`, `/backend`, `/tester`
